// A label is how the rest of the document points at an element, which in HTML
// is the id.

--- labeled-paragraph ---
A paragraph. <intro>
│ <p><span id="intro">A paragraph.</span></p>

--- labeled-heading ---
= Title <title>
│ <h1 id="title">Title</h1>

--- heading-label-is-generated ---
// Every heading carries a label: one derived from its text when the source
// wrote none, so that there is always an anchor to link a section by.
= Getting Started
│ <h1 id="getting-started">Getting Started</h1>

--- heading-label-deduplicated ---
= Same

= Same
│ <h1 id="same">Same</h1>
│ <h1 id="same-1">Same</h1>

--- labeled-list ---
- apples
- pears
<fruit>
│ <ul>
│ <li>apples</li>
│ <li id="fruit">pears</li>
│ </ul>

--- labeled-strong ---
A *bold* word. <p>
│ <p>A <strong>bold</strong> <span id="p">word.</span></p>
